# rm231, the dry peg (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm231
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_signe_brineworth
written_by codex
title the dry peg
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer honesty=frank
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk tests_a_sheltered_peg_at_the_end_of_a_shower
likes pickled_herring dice full_larder autumn_wind
dislikes waiting gulls
fears a_week_spent_waiting
hopes room_for_a_spare_shelf
topics weather +0.6 food +0.4 work +0.3 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=plain gossip=brisk refuse=flat tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# puts a peg within reach of a dripping eave and makes the time before the last drop pay for itself.

words
oath! = Split my best basket | Seven little gulls
saying! = A dry peg earns its hook | Count the jars with the lids off
peg = my spare peg | the little wooden clip
shelf = the back shelf | the narrow ledge
die = a square bone die | a cube of horn
pips = the black dots | those little holes
jar = the herring crock | a salt-stained jar
cover = a folded cloth | the heavy lid
gull = a pale thief | a white-winged nuisance
autumn = a rough autumn blow | the first leaf-stripping gale
larders = rows of jars | covered crocks
rinse = clean rinse water | the last clear dip
ticket = a bit of knotted string | a little tally of knots
rest = the length of one good stretch | five quiet breaths

any
opinion @1 houses against 1 : When a House raises rent on a place with a rotten sill I'd have the cost of the draught deducted.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : Don't weigh me the crock and charge the whole lot as fish.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : There's somewhere down our way to rest a basket without getting ordered off the step.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Some weeks there's more month than bread. A share from the dole covers the difference.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : Boots on the stairs at night. I'd like those to mean help more often.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : I'll take the windfall of a day off. Folk can have my place in the procession.

grown
line @1 greet : Right. You've got my attention and both my ears. | There's a minute going spare. Hello.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : You'll find me quite plain-spoken. | First time seeing you. I'll do you the courtesy of listening.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The morning has hardly been used yet. | Clean start today. Good morning.
line @1 greet.return : Yes, hello. I've put down what I was carrying. | Heard you first go. Glad to see you.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You don't add an ounce to the load, coming by. | Good. Somebody who understands a short visit.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Allow me one twist of the wrist. There. Hello. | I can keep working with company.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=night] : There's still a greeting left in me this late. | Last hello for the day, most likely.
line @1 again.open : We've time to finish what we started. | Back before the peg's gone dry.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Come alongside for the length of this street. | A bit of your company would suit me.
line @1 farewell : Get the easiest part of the road if you can. | Off you go while the going's good.
line @1 farewell.return : Yes. Plenty to have been going on with. | That lets us both get on.
line @1 react.news : Straight through to what happened, please. | I'll take the plain account, whatever it is.
line @1 react.news.new : I'd been going about my day quite ignorant of that. | That's come across my sill for the first time.
line @1 react.news.known : Heard it already and don't grudge the second hearing. | Yes. All the same pieces as before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Somebody's wrung that one a little too hard. | Doesn't feel like it's come to us straight.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice] : There's good hearing after a wearing stretch. | Fine news. I can feel my shoulders coming down.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|crime|theft|assault] : That'll leave a hollow place in somebody. Come rest. | Poor souls. There's no short way through a bit of news like that.
line @1 ask.how : Been able to put the load down at all today? | How's the day used you so far?
line @1 answer.how : Quite worn and quite capable of one more thing. | I'll do well enough after a sit and a bite.
line @1 sympathise : A hard day, even said quickly. I heard you. | No wonder you're spent. Give that parcel here.
line @1 reassure : We've a little in reserve for a day like this. | The time to rest has come round. Take it.
line @1 decline : I'd sooner disappoint you now and save you the wait. | I can't get it done in the time you've got.
line @1 accept_decline : Then I'll cross it off and get on. | That's clear. Saves two journeys.
line @1 thank : You spared me a long idle spell. Much obliged. | That's one bit I can lay aside. I owe you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It fitted into a gap in the day. | It only took two idle paws.
line @1 preclose : There's a little daylight I could still use. | I've got the next thing on my mind already.
line @1 accept_preclose : Take the minute before somebody else claims it. | Quite right. I'll pick up my own things.
scene peg_sign
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep one peg where the eave drips on it. | I'm watching a slip of wood for a weather report.
b : What can you tell by a wet peg? | Why watch that particular slip?
a : When the top dries the eave's done dripping. I can stand under it then. | I can see dark wood turn pale from well inside a dry doorway.

scene kind_of_wait
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I can wait hours if I'm free to do something else. | It's being kept ready that wears me thin.
b : Like standing with a basket on your hip? | Harder than it sounds.
a : Exactly. You can carry it somewhere or put it down. Halfway is hard on the back. | Yes. Tell me a time, then I can use what's left.

scene short_game
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fancy a game I can finish in three throws. | I'll roll for the largest number in three.
b : What do we put up? | What would a win get me?
a : First choice of the seat out of the draught. | The pick of these seats. That's about as much as I'll stake.

scene spots
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Bone dice ought to have the spots sunk deep. | I like a die I could read in the dark.
b : Planning to play without a lamp? | You read them by touch?
a : I might. No use wasting oil if everybody can count by paw. | Scrape of a claw and you know your score. Harder to rub a spot off too.

scene herring_break
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : For a short meal I'll have cold herring from my crock. | Nothing between my dinner and me but the lid of the herring jar.
b : Straight from the brine? | No bread with that?
a : Drain it first. A crust underneath soaks up what gets past my fork. | A heel of bread makes a good plate if you're short of both.

scene floor_level
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like my lowest shelf a good span above the floor. | A dry sack starts with a shelf up off the boards.
b : Damp comes through that far? | Surely the goods are in jars?
a : Not all days. Only takes one wet day to spoil a sack. | Fish in jars, meal in sacks. I like them all high and plainly visible.

scene full_shelf
when topic=dreams self.likes=full_larder
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : If I could add one thing at home it'd be a whole empty shelf. | I'd dearly like a bit more bare space in my larder.
b : Thought you liked full shelves. | Why keep one empty?
a : For moving the jars onto while I wipe the others. Full's fine, packed solid's a nuisance. | I set things there and count what's missing before I go out.

scene basket_count
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Each basket still to go gets one knot in my string. | #ticket.capitalize# keeps the count while I work.
b : Do you tie a lot of knots? | Which end do you start from?
a : Only at the start. Going home with a straight bit of string feels agreeable. | Nearest my paw. The point's to undo the lot before I set off.

scene clean_water
when topic=work self.job=laborer self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Clean work can make awfully dirty water. | You ever looked in a basin after the last rinse?
b : All of that came off one bundle? | Looks like the bottom of the harbour.
a : More than you'd think can hide in a fold. | At the start, yes. At the finish the bottom ought to show clear.

scene gull_meal
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'd sooner eat under a leaking roof than in sight of a gull. | Hate those clever eyes on my dinner.
b : Does covering the dish work? | Must be good herring.
a : Lid on, yes. Lid off to take a bite, you've an audience. | Probably. I should like a leisurely bite to judge for myself.

scene autumn_wood
when topic=weather self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rough autumn wind gets into every corner of a stair. | At least a proper draught can accomplish something.
b : Clears the cobwebs? | What job would you give it?
a : Cobwebs, stale smells, puddles under a rail. A whole free morning's work. | Drying every sodden doorstep between here and my own door.

scene feast_shelf
when topic=festival
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd serve the first share of a feast on little plates. | Small helpings to start and more in the pot.
b : Cutting the cost? | Would little plates make enough?
a : Getting a hot taste to the last hungry wolf before the keen appetites come round again. | The plates don't make supper. They give the late folk a chance at some.

scene one_stamp
when topic=prices
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : When a jar costs extra I want the jar for keeps. | A seller who wants the crock back can take a deposit.
b : Worth fussing over a crock? | What's a few coppers?
a : A crock a week is about a shelf of money by winter. | Depends which side of the counter you're on. I'll have mine back.

scene tired_truth
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A tired wolf looks put out whatever's on the mind inside. | Don't build a quarrel out of a long face.
b : Speaking from experience? | You know that for certain?
a : I've mistaken a backache for a grudge and made a fool of myself. | About my own face, yes. Sometimes it means I need the weight off my feet.

scene friend_pause
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'd share a quiet doorstep with #self.friend#. | I've a whole class of visits reserved for #self.friend#.
b : How long would a visit take? | Without a word between you?
a : A bite of herring and a look at the weather. That would do me. | If we liked. I'd certainly offer the fish first.

scene neighbour_window
when topic=home self.neighbour
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd set a dry peg by for #self.neighbour# if the weather looked doubtful. | There'd be room under my eave for #self.neighbour#.
b : Going to rain, is it? | What use is that in fair weather?
a : It'll come in handy whenever the rain does come. | I'll take my chances on another shower in this city.

scene church_door
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A seat out of the weather goes well with prayer. | I like a seat near the chapel door.
b : Need to get out quick? | Is that for the breeze?
a : To shift along quick when somebody comes in with aching feet. | That's one reason. Easier to make room for a late arrival too.

scene vineyard_slip
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Words on paper showed me how a vineyard hill curves. | I've kept a little description of vines tied up in rows.
b : Never seen the vines yourself? | Fine words, are they?
a : Wouldn't know the hill on sight. I might know where to sit on it to eat. | Ordinary ones. That's why I can picture the mud on the writer's boots.

story six_dice [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I once rolled three dice at the same time and managed to lose the lot. Had the tabletop all to myself too.
  : I'd set it on a slant to drain the rinse water. Those dice went straight down my apron front.
  b : What was the score?
  : One bruise on my foot and three clean dice. I called that even.

story crock_journey [topic=food|memories]
  : I carried a covered herring crock home cradled against my ribs. Took such care not a drop went over the rim.
  : It had a small crack underneath. My coat smelled of the sea for days.
  b : Were there gulls?
  : You'd have taken me for a travelling fish market when I finally fetched up at home.

story hanging_wait [topic=weather|memories]
  : Once I watched for rain to stop so long I got annoyed at the sound of every drop. Sky was bright, too.
  : Went out and looked up. The drops were off a sodden sheet hung over the rail above me.
  b : What did you do?
  : Wrung the corner. Had my clear weather very promptly after that.

rule @drops
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Belly of the peg's pale now. Almost done dripping. | Drop, pause, drop again. Plenty of time for a bite.

rule @break
when concept=bark self.likes=dice
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One throw apiece while there's a seat, anyone? | No stakes bar the driest seat in reach!

rule @work
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=laborer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One more knot undone. That's progress. | Easy on the load while I get my hip under it.

rule @swindler
when concept=bark self.dislikes=gulls
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Get your beak away. Nobody ordered company with this meal. | My fish. Pick on somebody with fish to spare.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I'll hear what you came for. Might sit down while I do.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, caught me with a minute I hadn't promised to anyone.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : State what you want with a sensible distance between us.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=dawn] : Still a bit of yesterday in my bones. I can listen.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=laborer] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. My knee could tell you how heavy a basket is.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work steady till it's done, then lay it aside till I'm needed.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Leave while the doorstep's clear.
graft resident.hub
choice What makes that an especially good peg? -> pegmark
node pegmark
say It's dark on one side from all those times the eave dripped on it. I can tell the wet half by touch when the light's poor.
free
choice Have you ever lost it? -> lostwood
choice I see the mark. -> hub
node lostwood
say Once. Borrowed another. Watched it through a whole meal before I saw somebody'd painted the thing brown on both sides.
choice Back to something else. -> hub
choice Good drying weather to you. -> bye
